Package: live-radio
Version: 1.1.2
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: Live Radio <live-radio@example.invalid>
Installed-Size: 7200
Depends: mpv, curl, libc6 (>= 2.28), libx11-6, libx11-xcb1, libxcursor1, libxrandr2, libxi6, libxrender1, libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libwayland-client0, libwayland-cursor0, libwayland-egl1, libegl1, libgl1
Recommends: pipewire | pulseaudio
Description: Live radio for your Raspberry Pi - no account, one tap to play
 Live Radio is a lightweight desktop radio player for Raspberry Pi OS.
 It plays hundreds of live AM and FM stations from across the US in
 more than 40 genres: Top 40, country, rock, hip-hop, news, sports,
 Spanish-language and more. No account or sign-in is needed.
 .
 Features:
  - One-tap play with the current song or show title
  - Browse by genre, or search by name, call sign, city or frequency
  - Real station logos, cached for instant loading
  - Favourites and recently played stations
  - Automatic portrait layout for rotated screens and touchscreens
  - Full-screen mode (live-radio --fullscreen) for kiosk setups
  - Volume and mute remembered between sessions; Space to play/pause
 .
 Live Radio is an independent player, not affiliated with or endorsed
 by iHeartMedia. It plays the public live streams stations publish
 online. Audio playback is handled by mpv.
